API-02: shift the trace node index when a junction is added

EN_addnode shifts every tank and reservoir up one place when it adds a
junction, but not quality.TraceNode, so a trace from a tank or
reservoir silently runs from a different node. The shift was added by
PR #829 (commit a5bce31) and lost two days later when commit 7a16739
(PR #831) overwrote epanet.c. This restores it, next to the shift of
the Tank array and with the same test that is used for links.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-02_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..f0ccb4c 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1975,6 +1975,8 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addnode(EN_Project p, const char *id, int nodeType, int *index)
         {
             net->Tank[i].Node += 1;
         }
+        // shift index of water quality trace node, if necessary
+        if (qual->TraceNode > net->Njuncs - 1) qual->TraceNode += 1;
         // shift indices of Links, if necessary
         for (i = 1; i <= net->Nlinks; i++)
         {
